# Copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in. Only the provider you use needs a key.

# --- Easiest: OpenAI's API for every model -------------------------------------------
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# BENCH_PROVIDER=openai               # the default

# --- Or: Azure OpenAI ------------------------------------------------------------------
# BENCH_PROVIDER=azure
# AZURE_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://<your-resource>.openai.azure.com/openai/v1
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY=...
# Deployment names differ per account; map each model to yours:
# BENCH_MODEL_ID_GPT_6_LUNA=my-luna-deployment

# --- Or: AWS Bedrock (OpenAI-compatible endpoint, Bedrock API key) ---------------------
# BENCH_PROVIDER=bedrock
# BEDROCK_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://bedrock-runtime.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/openai/v1
# AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=...

# --- Or: any OpenAI-compatible gateway (LiteLLM, OpenRouter, your proxy) ---------------
# BENCH_PROVIDER=compatible
# COMPATIBLE_BASE_URL=https://my-gateway.example.com/v1
# COMPATIBLE_API_KEY=...

# --- Mixing providers -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Any single model can use a different provider and ID. <MODEL> is the model name upper-cased,
# with - and . replaced by _ (gpt-5.6-sol -> GPT_5_6_SOL). This study ran GPT-6 on Bedrock and the
# legacy model on Azure, because Bedrock does not return logprobs:
# BENCH_PROVIDER_GPT_5_6_SOL=azure
# BENCH_MODEL_ID_GPT_5_6_SOL=gpt-5.6
